  "articleBody": "Nobody wants a beautiful new bathroom countertop to go wrong, right? There are definitely a few common pitfalls folks encounter during installation, and knowing them can save you a lot of headaches. One biggie is inaccurate measurements. Walls aren't always perfectly square, and if you don't account for that, or your sink and faucet locations, you could end up with a top that just doesn't fit right. It's why professional templating is so important! Another mistake is picking a material that doesn't quite match your lifestyle. Marble, for instance, is gorgeous but needs a bit more TLC than, say, quartz, especially in a busy family bathroom. Understand its care requirements before committing! Then there's the issue of inadequate support. If your vanity isn't level or there's not enough shimming, your stone countertop could be under stress and even crack down the line. Proper leveling and support are crucial. And don't forget about sealing and caulking. Poorly sealed edges or a gap in the caulk around the sink or backsplash can lead to water seeping in, causing all sorts of damage like swelling or mold. Finally, it's essential to clarify all the details before fabrication—cutouts, edge details, backsplash height. Surprises on install day are never fun! Working with experienced pros like us helps ensure these details are handled perfectly the first time. Reach out if you're planning a countertop refresh!",
